            <ArticleTitle>[Chronic ulnar wrist pain in adults: diagnosis and treatment principles].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>313-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.main.2011.09.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adult patients with chronic ulnar wrist pain often seek medical advice. There are a number of diagnoses for chronic ulnar-sided wrist pain. A sound diagnostic strategy is therefore of paramount importance. Patient's history, clinical examination and high quality standard radiographs are the most important part of this strategy. Sophisticated investigations should only be performed to focus on solid clinical hypotheses. The palmar and dorsal aetiologies of ulnar wrist pain are considered as well as their treatment principles.</AbstractText>
